From cc4b777f2feebad0c8823f438f94a473642f3a10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PRIME B360M-C port <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:45:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] util/intelp2m: Add Cannon Lake PCH-H platform

The `cnl` platform models Cannon Lake PCH-LP, where only community 0
(GPP_A, GPP_B, GPP_G) uses the PWROK/DEEP/PLTRST/RSMRST encoding of
PADRSTCFG and every other community, including GPD, uses
RSMRST/DEEP/PLTRST.

Cannon Lake PCH-H (300-series desktop chipsets such as B360/H370/Q370)
is the other way around: all GPP communities use RSMRST/DEEP/PLTRST and
only the GPD community uses PWROK/DEEP/PLTRST/RSMRST, as described by
rst_map and rst_map_gpd in soc/intel/cannonlake/gpio_cnp_h.c. Running
`-p cnl` on a PCH-H inteltool dump therefore yields wrong reset sources
for GPP_A, GPP_B, GPP_G and GPD pads.

Add a `cnl-h` platform that reuses the Cannon Lake register decoding and
only overrides the reset source remapping, plus a test for both
encodings.

TEST=go test ./... in util/intelp2m

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
